Settling a thread leaves the timer where it was.
A thread alone on the processor that loses its units would run on to a count the timer was set to for it alone;
the timer is set past a count only while no change since has brought that count forward.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets a turn on spare time run past its span while another waits
Witness: fuzz actor-handoff

